{"abstract":[{"text":"Show a Markdown document in a SwiftUI view, and adapt it to light and dark mode.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DisplayingMarkdownWithSwiftUI"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"MarkdownKit"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Displaying Markdown with SwiftUI"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI comes with support for Markdown-formatted snippets but does not have a full-fledged viewer for Markdown documents. MarkdownKit includes a SwiftUI view for displaying Markdown documents. As opposed to many other custom created Markdown views, the one included in MarkdownKit is based on the CommonMark-compliant MarkdownKit parser as well as its attributed string generator. It is thus lightweight yet still quite configurable. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is available on macOS 14 and iOS 17 or later.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The initializer of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" receives the parsed Markdown content of type ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", an optional ","type":"text"},{"code":"waitingMessage:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter which defines what is being displayed while the content is being rendered (especially if many images need to be loaded), as well as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"generator:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter defining how the parsed Markdown is transformed into an attributed string, which is then being shown in the view. The generator is not just called once, but every time the color scheme has changed to potentially update the colors in use.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A variant of this initializer accepts a Markdown document as a string and parses it with the standard parser of a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownDialect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": the ","type":"text"},{"code":"dialect:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter selects it, and the default is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownDialect/extendedCommonMark","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownDialect/fullMath","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" if you pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"math:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", see below). Pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"dialect: .full","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the syntax of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"dialect: .fullLaTeX","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for formulas with the delimiters ","type":"text"},{"code":"\\(…\\)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"\\[…\\]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/LaTeXMarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). There are two initializers for each of the two ways of providing the document. Either you pass a ","type":"text"},{"code":"generator:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or you do not provide one and the view uses the default generators for light and dark mode, which can be configured with ","type":"text"},{"code":"renderingOptions:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; the default is ","type":"text"},{"code":".trusted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"code":"mermaid:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"math:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"style:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"darkStyle:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/Style-swift.struct","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for light and dark mode (the defaults are ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/Style-swift.struct/default","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/Style-swift.struct/dark","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following code snippet shows the signatures of the initializers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct MarkdownText: View {","  init(_ text: Block,","       waitingMessage: NSAttributedString = NSAttributedString(string: \"⏳\"),","       renderingOptions: AttributedStringGenerator.RenderingOptions = .trusted,","       mermaid: MermaidConfig? = nil,","       math: MathConfig? = nil) {","    ...","  }","  init(_ text: Block,","       waitingMessage: NSAttributedString = NSAttributedString(string: \"⏳\"),","       generator: ((Block, ColorScheme) -> NSAttributedString?)?,","       prepare: (@Sendable (Block, ColorScheme) async -> Bool)? = nil) {","    ...","  }","  init(string: String,","       dialect: MarkdownDialect? = nil,","       waitingMessage: NSAttributedString = NSAttributedString(string: \"⏳\"),","       renderingOptions: AttributedStringGenerator.RenderingOptions = .trusted,","       mermaid: MermaidConfig? = nil,","       math: MathConfig? = nil) {","    ...","  }","  init(string: String,","       dialect: MarkdownDialect? = nil,","       waitingMessage: NSAttributedString = NSAttributedString(string: \"⏳\"),","       generator: ((Block, ColorScheme) -> NSAttributedString?)?,","       prepare: (@Sendable (Block, ColorScheme) async -> Bool)? = nil) {","    ...","  }","  ...","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Keep-untrusted-content-in-check","level":3,"text":"Keep untrusted content in check","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The view generates the attributed string synchronously, which is why only the rendering options ","type":"text"},{"code":"baseUrl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"localImages","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"imageExtensions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"safeMode","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"textSizeMultiplier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" have an effect (remote images are never loaded). Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"MarkdownText(string: text, renderingOptions: .untrusted)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if the Markdown does not come from a trusted source. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/RenderingUntrustedMarkdown","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Show-Mermaid-diagrams","level":3,"text":"Show Mermaid diagrams","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"mermaid: .default","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to draw diagrams. The view first shows the code of a diagram and replaces it with the diagram once it has been rendered in the background. In dark mode, it uses ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MermaidConfig/darkVariant","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Show-formulas","level":3,"text":"Show formulas","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"math: MathConfig()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to show LaTeX formulas as images. A string is parsed with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MathMarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownDialect/fullMath","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") then, unless you pass another ","type":"text"},{"code":"dialect:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Like diagrams, the formulas are rendered in the background: the view first shows the LaTeX as code. In dark mode, the formulas are white (the colour of the text). See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MathematicalFormulas","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Align-the-markers-of-lists","level":3,"text":"Align the markers of lists","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The system’s HTML importer turns lists into tables whose cells are laid out at their top, so the number or bullet of a list item is above the text if an image, such as a formula, makes the first line of the item taller than the text. ","type":"text"},{"code":"MarkdownText(…, alignListMarkers: true)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" puts the markers on the baseline of the first line of their items: after every layout, also when the window is resized or the device is rotated, it measures the layout of its text view and lowers the markers with the character attribute ","type":"text"},{"code":"baselineOffset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". On iOS it needs the text system of TextKit 1 (which lists need anyway), and it costs time for long texts, so it is off by default. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/alignListMarkers","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" does it when a generator creates the string, without knowing the width of the text, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Foundation/NSAttributedString/preparedForRTFD()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" always does it, since RTFD viewers lay out lowered images differently than a text view does.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Customize-the-generators-for-light-and-dark-mode","level":3,"text":"Customize the generators for light and dark mode","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To change the fonts, colors or spacing of the default generators, pass a style for each mode. A style does not need a generator of your own:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var style = AttributedStringGenerator.Style.default","style.fontFamily = \"Georgia, serif\"","var darkStyle = AttributedStringGenerator.Style.dark","darkStyle.fontFamily = \"Georgia, serif\"","MarkdownText(string: text, style: style, darkStyle: darkStyle)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass a ","type":"text"},{"code":"generator:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if you need more, such as a subclass of the generator. Here is an example how view ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" could be used in a simple Markdown viewer. It defines an attributed string generator that uses two color schemes depending on whether dark mode is active or not.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct ContentView: View {","  private static let lightGenerator = AttributedStringGenerator()","  private static let darkGenerator = AttributedStringGenerator(","      fontColor: \"#FFF\", codeFontColor: \"#FFF\",","      codeBlockFontColor: \"#FF6\", codeBlockBackground: \"#333\",","      syntaxHighlighting: .defaultDark,","      borderColor: \"#BBB\", h1Color: \"#FFF\", h2Color: \"#FFF\",","      h3Color: \"#FFF\", h4Color: \"#FFF\")","  ","  let content = ExtendedMarkdownParser.standard.parse(\"\"\"","    Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, **consectetur adipiscing** elit. Aliquam","    non risus in massa ornare lacinia. _Etiam_ at ullamcorper ligula.","    ","    1. This is the first item","    2. This is the second item","    3. This is the third item","    ","    Cras laoreet tellus dolor, ac `suscipit augue` molestie a.","    Integer efficitur odio massa, in dictum arcu dictum in.","    ","    | Column 1           | Column 2          | Col 3 |","    | ------------------ | ----------------- | :---: |","    | Nunc at dignissim  | More `cell` text  | One   |","    | Integer **ligula** | Justo nec finibus | Two   |","    | Cras nibh ex       | Praesent congue   | Three |","    \"\"\")","  ","  var body: some View {","    MarkdownText(self.content) { doc, colorScheme in","      switch colorScheme {","        case .dark:","          return Self.darkGenerator.generate(doc: doc)","        default:","          return Self.lightGenerator.generate(doc: doc)","      }","    }","    .padding()","  }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Prepare-diagrams-and-formulas-for-custom-generators","level":3,"text":"Prepare diagrams and formulas for custom generators","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A custom ","type":"text"},{"code":"generator:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called synchronously, so it can only show Mermaid diagrams and formulas which have been rendered before. The default generators render them in the background and generate the text again once they are ready. To get the same with your own generators, pass a ","type":"text"},{"code":"prepare:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function: the view calls it after it has shown the text for the first time, for each document and color scheme, and generates the text again if it returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct ContentView: View {","  private static let lightGenerator = MathAttributedStringGenerator(mermaid: .default)","  private static let darkGenerator = MathAttributedStringGenerator(","      fontColor: \"#FFF\", codeFontColor: \"#FFF\", mermaid: MermaidConfig.default.darkVariant)","  ","  let content = MathMarkdownParser.standard.parse(\"The area is $\\\\pi r^2$.\")","  ","  var body: some View {","    MarkdownText(self.content, generator: { doc, colorScheme in","      let generator = colorScheme == .dark ? Self.darkGenerator : Self.lightGenerator","      return generator.generate(doc: doc)","    }, prepare: { doc, colorScheme in","      let generator = colorScheme == .dark ? Self.darkGenerator : Self.lightGenerator","      let diagrams = await generator.prepareDiagrams(in: doc)","      let formulas = await generator.prepareMath(in: doc)","      return diagrams || formulas","    })","    .padding()","  }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit":{"abstract":[{"text":"Parse, process and display text in Markdown format.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"MarkdownKit","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator":{"abstract":[{"code":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides functionality for converting Markdown blocks into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSAttributedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects that are used in macOS and iOS for displaying rich text.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The implementation is extensible allowing subclasses of ","type":"text"},{"code":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"override how individual Markdown structures are converted into attributed strings.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"}],"role":"symbol","title":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct":{"abstract":[{"text":"Options for rendering the HTML that ","type":"text"},{"code":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" generates into an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSAttributedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". They are used by the synchronous methods (","type":"text"},{"code":"generate(doc:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" etc.) as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"well as by the asynchronous ones (","type":"text"},{"code":"generateAsync(doc:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" etc.).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RenderingOptions"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RenderingOptions"}],"role":"symbol","title":"AttributedStringGenerator.RenderingOptions","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator/renderingoptions-swift.struct"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/Style-swift.struct":{"abstract":[{"text":"The appearance of the attributed strings that a generator creates: fonts, colors, spacing,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"borders, the size of images, the syntax highlighting theme, and CSS of your own.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Style"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/Style-swift.struct","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Style"}],"role":"symbol","title":"AttributedStringGenerator.Style","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator/style-swift.struct"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/Style-swift.struct/dark":{"abstract":[{"text":"Colors for a dark background, whatever the appearance of the system is: white text, light","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"blue code on dark gray code blocks, red and blue headings, and the syntax highlighting theme","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for dark backgrounds. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" uses it in dark mode.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dark"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC5StyleV","text":"Style"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/Style-swift.struct/dark","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"dark","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator/style-swift.struct/dark"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/Style-swift.struct/default":{"abstract":[{"text":"The style of a generator that is created without one: the colors of the system, for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"appearance (light or dark) at the time when they are first used.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"`default`"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC5StyleV","text":"Style"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/Style-swift.struct/default","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"default","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator/style-swift.struct/default"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/alignListMarkers":{"abstract":[{"text":"If true, the numbers and bullets of list items sit on the baseline of the first line of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their items, also if an image (such as a formula) makes that line taller than the text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(macOS and iOS; the default is ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"alignListMarkers"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/alignListMarkers","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"alignListMarkers","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator/alignlistmarkers"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block":{"abstract":[{"text":"Enumeration of Markdown blocks. This enumeration defines the block structure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"i.e. the abstract syntax, of Markdown supported by MarkdownKit. The structure of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inline text is defined by the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" struct.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Block"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Block"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Block","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/block"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/CustomizingAttributedStringOutput":{"abstract":[{"text":"Style the attributed strings that ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" creates, and understand what the system’s HTML importer does with the styles.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/CustomizingAttributedStringOutput","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Customizing Attributed String Output","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/customizingattributedstringoutput"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams":{"abstract":[{"text":"Show fenced code blocks with the language ","type":"text"},{"code":"mermaid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as diagrams in attributed strings.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Drawing Mermaid Diagrams","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/drawingmermaiddiagrams"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ExtendedMarkdownParser":{"abstract":[{"code":"ExtendedMarkdownParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects are used to parse Markdown text represented as a string","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"using all extensions to the CommonMark specification implemented by MarkdownKit.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ExtendedMarkdownParser"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ExtendedMarkdownParser","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ExtendedMarkdownParser"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ExtendedMarkdownParser","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/extendedmarkdownparser"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Foundation/NSAttributedString/preparedForRTFD()":{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns a copy of the attributed string whose image attachments the RTFD format represents","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"faithfully. Use it before you export an attributed string with images, such as the diagrams","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and formulas of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MathAttributedStringGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", as an RTFD document","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"fileWrapper(from:documentAttributes:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the document type ","type":"text"},{"code":"rtfd","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). This is what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/rtfd(_:title:author:maxImageWidth:renderingOptions:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" does.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"prep